  "transcript": "There's a scene in Fullmetal Alchemist where Shu Tucker faces losing his funding and status as a state alchemist and out of pure desperation to produce new research, attempts to combine his daughter and his dog to produce a talking chimera. And the darkest part of it all was that it actually worked. AI companies are constantly pushing new frontiers in the race against others and other country governments. The race to AGI has become glamorized around the world. Pair this with the general consensus of publish or perish within academia and the social and financial pressures to join the biggest AI labs in the world and earn professional athlete type salaries and it is no surprise that many people in the AI field are drunk with the pursuit of winning this endless race. The biggest question is no longer can I do this, it is should I do this. Unfortunately, Ed and Al were unaware of the work Tucker was doing to fuse his daughter and his dog together. But we currently see what's happening in front of our own eyes. With crazy cyber attacks happening basically every single week and many headlines calling for all the bells to be rung. Despite this, more incentives seem to be getting created to push on with IPOs and new seed rounds being pushed every single day. I'm all for the advancement of technology. It has been embedded in the history of mankind. But we need to be wary of the reason of why we're doing some of this and truly ask ourselves, why should this even be built in the first place?"
}]